        ["app.subtitle"] = "PlayStation controllers on Windows",
        ["nav.guide"] = "Guide", ["guide.title"] = "Quick guide",
        ["guide.1.t"] = "1. Connect the controller", ["guide.1.b"] = "Plug the DualSense, DualSense Edge or DualShock 4 in with a USB cable, or pair it over Bluetooth: hold PS + Create (PS + Share on DS4) until the light blinks and add it in Windows Settings → Bluetooth & devices. It appears on the Home page with its battery and connection.",
        ["guide.2.t"] = "2. Playing games (emulation)", ["guide.2.b"] = "Many PC games only understand Xbox controllers. Install ViGEmBus (button in Emulation & connections) and choose “Emulate as Xbox 360” or “DualShock 4”. So games don't see two controllers, also install HidHide and tick “Hide controllers while they are being emulated”.",
        ["guide.3.t"] = "3. Adaptive triggers", ["guide.3.b"] = "On the Adaptive triggers page pick a mode (or a preset such as Pistol, Bow or Brake) for L2 and R2. The graph shows where the trigger gets stiff and the white line shows your finger live. Compatible game mods drive the triggers themselves over UDP port 6969.",
        ["guide.4.t"] = "4. Light, rumble and haptics", ["guide.4.b"] = "Under Lighting set the lightbar colour and player LEDs. Under Rumble & haptics turn game rumble or PC audio into HD haptics (USB and Bluetooth) and try the test patterns. You can also play PC audio on the controller speaker there, wired or over Bluetooth.",
        ["guide.5.t"] = "5. Touchpad as mouse", ["guide.5.b"] = "Double tap or rest a finger on the touchpad: the controller ticks twice and the touchpad outline turns green. One finger moves the cursor, press to click (right side = right click), tap to click, two fingers scroll. To turn it off, hold the click for 5 seconds or stop touching for a few seconds.",
        ["guide.6.t"] = "6. Gyroscope", ["guide.6.b"] = "In Keyboard, mouse & macros you can aim by moving the controller: “Move the cursor with: Gyroscope” for mouse games, or “Gyro as right stick” for games that only take a controller. Put the controller on the desk and click “Calibrate gyro” if aim drifts. “Player space” keeps aim right even with the controller tilted.",
        ["guide.7.t"] = "7. Buttons, macros and turbo", ["guide.7.b"] = "Any button can become a key, mouse click or macro (e.g. “ctrl+c”). Use activators to give one button two jobs (tap, double tap or hold), the Shift layer for a second set of buttons while you hold one, and Turbo for rapid fire.",
        ["guide.8.t"] = "8. Per-game profiles", ["guide.8.b"] = "Everything you change is stored in the selected profile. In Game library find your Steam, Epic and GOG games and create a profile for each: when the game opens, AuroraPad switches profile by itself. Shortcut: PS + Options / PS + Create go to the next / previous profile.",
        ["guide.9.t"] = "9. PS button shortcuts", ["guide.9.b"] = "Hold PS and press: Options/Create = switch profile, touchpad = toggle keyboard & mouse, △ = pause the virtual controller, ▲/▼ = lightbar brightness, Mute = show battery on the lightbar. A quick tap on PS alone still reaches the game.",
